components": "Allow different phases of animation, carousel slides, video frames, transient promotional widgets and consent states when the surrounding component and page remain coherent. Use visible context such as slide indicators, component boundaries and related text to recognize these roles. A different frame or slide alone is not content loss or incoherent evidence. Do not assume every broken image or empty main section is an animation.", "external_embeds": "An unavailable third-party video, social widget or auxiliary embed alone is not a material defect when the surrounding page still communicates its information and supports its purpose. Assess its contextual role: missing sole essential instructions or content is different from an optional supplementary player. Do not require a remote service to operate from the saved reproduction.", "scroll_context": "Inspect ALL supplied reference and target segments. Align corresponding content, not identical offsets. Normal viewport cuts, scroll-boundary overlap, sticky headers and differences in page height are not by themselves permanent content loss. Distinguish these from substantial overlap or clipping that renders core content unreadable. Do not infer source content missing merely because reference coverage is shorter.", "material_defects": "Require observable impact on core information, understanding or essential visible controls: a blank/blocked main interface, materially incoherent text, substantial unreadability or overlap, repeated broken editorial/product imagery, or an essential control whose label/purpose is not understandable. Ignore minor cosmetic imperfections. Existing accessibility-tool violations alone do not imply failure.", "evidence_coherence": "Assess whether the supplied states belong to the intended reference/target comparison under its category and form a coherent assessable set. A permissible dynamic, advertising or regenerated-layout difference is not incoherence. Evaluate localized content/